    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the Austin Waves is anchored by the elite 83.85 score of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who draws a favorable matchup against Trevor Rogers. His proximity to the top of the lineup and a significant park factor boost make him our must-start anchor. Alongside him, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Nasim Nunez** (64.14) represent our strongest plays against Lucas Giolito. Both benefit from a soft SP_xERA of 5.37, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically seeing a substantial bump from a +14% platoon advantage that vaults him into our \"Strong\" tier. **Sam Antonacci** also warrants attention; despite a neutral park, his leadoff placement (+10% order bonus) and a high-upside matchup against Troy Melton produce a rock-solid 63.14 score.\n\nWe face notable resistance against high-end arms today, forcing a more conservative approach with core stars. **Gunnar Henderson** (53.01), **Andy Pages** (49.35), and **Kyle Tucker** (55.12) are all facing tough assignments against Adam Macko and Zack Wheeler, respectively. These sub-60 scores are elevated solely by their lineup positioning and, in **Kyle Tucker**'s case, favorable wind conditions; however, the SP_xERA for these matchups mandates cautious expectations. The tightest decision on the bench involved **Coby Mayo** (51.15), who missed the cut for the final utility spot. While his park and platoon edges were attractive, the Optimizer favored the higher floor of **Miguel Vargas** (59.00) due to his #3 lineup position and slightly more favorable historical output. With lineups still pending across the board, keep a close eye on the late-afternoon updates, as any drop in batting order for our marginal starters could push them below the 40-point bench threshold.",
